A||||5||JohnF||Oxygen Sensor for Tech 4||||1||
Z||000000||JohnF||11-03-2001||12:31 PM||||'88 auto.  ALDL recorded a reading of Code 13 only. <P>ENGINE light only on intermittantly after start. <P>Car very hard to get to start when hot.  Turns over fine, eventually smell of gas.  Then starts roughly, then smooths out and runs like new til next start.  Make sense (before I replace) 02 Sensor?||||reg||1
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||11-03-2001||12:58 PM||||The O2 sensor would be a good start but you might also want to consider a choked up cat. I believe that in past discussions a plugged cat will just toast the O2 sensor. <P>What did you mean that its hard to start? Does it turn over and over before firing off? Or is the starter itself just clicking without turning over?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnF||11-03-2001||08:48 PM||||Starter and engine turns over normally for about 20 seconds. After that, it may be nothing; it may be a sputtering sound.  Because of possible overheating, I quit.  After a pause for starter cooling, I try again.  After a few (3 - 4 tried), it has started roughly at first, then run beautifully.<P>Now, I get a code 44 to go with my 13.  Seems like 02 sensor all the way! Yes?||||reg||1
Z||000003||WKDFIRO||11-04-2001||04:34 PM||||I take it that the sputtering is coming from the starter? <P>In that case you just need to replace the starter. Heat really effects starters that are on their last legs.<P>Lean exhaust at the 02 sensor? (code 44) If the sensor hasn't been changed in a while it should be the culprit!||||reg||1
Z||000004||JohnF||11-04-2001||05:17 PM||||Thanks for the suggestions.  Replaced O2 Sensor.  Problem solved!  Easy starting - no ENGINE light.||||reg||10
